fact WorkItem(id: "WI-749", description: some(value: "WI-714 follow-up (F2): a ZERO-ARG member access on a rule-reference value ('person_row.isEmpty', 'Person.rows.isEmpty') is not re-routed to a dot call and fails loudly as 'isEmpty.name: expected resolved name, got unresolved'. CONTEXT: found by the /code-review pass on WI-729 (2026-07-18) and confirmed empirically. This is the ZERO-ARG dual of the method-call re-route, and it is INDEPENDENT of qualification: the bare-UNQUALIFIED 'person_row.isEmpty' fails too, so it predates WI-729 and is a WI-723/WI-280 gap, not a WI-729 regression. ROOT CAUSE (known precisely): WI-723 widened the METHOD-CALL receiver probe to accept a RULE (a rule reference IS a Relation[T] value, WI-714) -- load.rs dot_call_receiver falls back to resolve_qualified_rule_readonly -- but the FIELD-ACCESS path never got that widening: try_identifier_dot_field gates on field_access_root_is_value, which walks the chain to its root Ident and calls dot_receiver_binder, accepting ONLY a local binder / op param. A rule root returns None, so the chain stays a field_access, then try_qualified_rule_ref tries to resolve the WHOLE dotted name ('person_row.isEmpty') as a rule, which it is not, and it falls through to qualified-name flattening. NARROW + workaround-able: 'let r = person_row; r.isEmpty' works, so nothing is blocked -- only the inline zero-arg spelling. FIX DIRECTION: in try_identifier_dot_field (or field_access_root_is_value), when the receiver SUBCHAIN (everything but the final member) spells a name resolving to a rule via the shared read-only resolve_qualified_rule_readonly probe, build the zero-arg DotApply with the collapsed var_ref(Ref(rule)) receiver -- the same receiver dot_call_receiver synthesizes. Keep the Goal/Rule kind gate and the qualified_visible gate, and keep the LOCAL-value re-route ordered FIRST so a binder still shadows a same-named rule. Mind the ordering against try_qualified_rule_ref, which must still collapse a WHOLE-chain rule name ('Queen.find') to a bare reference. ACCEPTANCE: 'person_row.isEmpty' and 'Person.rows.isEmpty' load, type and EVAL equal to the let-bound spelling; a genuine field access on a local value still wins (no regression); a chain resolving to neither a local nor a rule stays the loud unknown-name error (no silent fallback); cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-729"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-18T08:53:00Z"))
